flowchart TD
    %% Send side
    ATTACH([User attaches a file to a message]) --> PICK[GUI picks the file · platform chooser]
PICK --> COPY[Core copies it into the store, or references it in place · keep-a-copy checkbox<br>block hashes → fileId]
COPY --> MSG[Publish message with attachment references<br>notification only — no key, no transfer params]
COPY --> CLASS{file class}
MSG --> CLASS
CLASS -- " small (≤ smallFileMaxBytes · a network value) " --> FAN[Seal registry fans out: one seal per device of the account<br>seal = fileId + block list + seal key, ratchet-encrypted to that device]
CLASS -- " large (no upper bound) " --> NOPUSH([nothing pushed · each device decides to pull])

FAN --> DIRECT[Direct transfer · OFFER carries the seal · tag FILE_TRANSFER]
DIRECT -- " OFFER ACKed " --> CHUNKS[Chunk rows in the outbox · windowed · messages go first<br>AEAD under the seal key · AAD = sealId, offset, length<br>chunk ACK = decrypted + durably staged]
DIRECT -- " DECLINED by the target " --> DEAD([seal DECLINED · refused for that device])
DIRECT -- " other terminal NACK " --> ENDEDM([transfer ENDED · REQUEST recovers with a fresh seal])
CHUNKS -- " every chunk held " --> DELIVERED((seal DELIVERED · live deposits cancelled))
CHUNKS -- " gone: link closed · no link · no chunk ACK at all for chunkAckTimeout " --> REM[Remainder = from the target's ACKed<br>contiguous prefix to the end]
DIRECT -- " gone before the ACK: no link · no ACK within relayBackupAfter " --> REM
REM --> DEPOSIT[One deposit round per seal · claimed durably<br>one transfer per relay RelaySelectionPolicy returns · same seal, same remainder]
DEPOSIT --> ADM{Relay admission<br>from the seal's origin · known target · within the pledge budget}
ADM -- DECLINED --> OUT([that relay is out · one jump<br>the origin never chases])
ADM -- admitted --> HOLD["Relay hop = an incoming transfer like any other<br>keeps only the seal bytes and chunk ciphertext<br>chunk outside the shape or for a dead hop → DECLINED"]
HOLD --> WHOLE{Every chunk stored?}
WHOLE -- " no, idle for fileRelayIdleTtl " --> TTL[hop dropped · never forwarded]
WHOLE -- yes --> HANDED((seal HANDED_OFF at the origin · direct push stops))
WHOLE -- yes --> FWD[Forward = an ordinary transfer to the final target<br>same seal bytes and shape · chunks read from the store]
FWD -- " DECLINED by the target (no space) " --> DROP([relay drops the hop · quota freed])
FWD -- " done " --> FORGET((relay forgets the hop))

%% Target side
CHUNKS -. delivered .-> TARGET
FWD -. delivered .-> TARGET
TARGET[Target: seal opened once · its row written at open<br>later hops of the same seal bind by sealId without decrypting]
TARGET --> MERGE[Receiver merges into fileId-scoped byte coverage<br>blocks verified at checkpoints → READY]
MERGE --> COMPLETE[READY → ACK everything to live hops · COMPLETE to each seal's origin]
COMPLETE -. " COMPLETE " .-> DELIVERED

    %% Pull path
    MSG -. "synced / processed by any device" .-> TRIG
TRIG{Message references a fileId · no complete local file ·<br>small: after filePullDelay · large: auto-download limit or user click} -- yes --> CAND[One candidate at a time · serve gate at the holder<br>sender devices, then own-account siblings]
CAND -- " small " --> REQ[REQUEST envelope · sealed, direct-only<br>ACK → waiting for the OFFER · DECLINED → next candidate]
CAND -- " large " --> PULL[Requester opens a WebRTC session and a file channel<br>PULL fileId + fromOffset = checkpointed P<br>PULL_OK with the block list · DECLINED → next candidate]
REQ -- " serve: a fresh seal " --> SERVE[Holder opens a transfer from the chunk boundary<br>at or below the requester's held prefix<br>checks each block as it reads]
SERVE -. delivered .-> TARGET
PULL -- " PULL_OK " --> STREAM[Holder sends plain DATA frames in order · block-checked<br>no envelope, no key, no transferId · DTLS protects the channel<br>PROGRESS at checkpoints · credit window · ends with the channel]
STREAM -. delivered .-> MERGE
STREAM -- " session dropped " --> CAND
PULL -- " no session possible " --> NOCONN([no direct connection · shown to the user · never over Tor])
NOPUSH -. " message lands " .-> TRIG
CAND -- " all declined " --> UNAV([file unavailable · re-openable])
MERGE -. " prefix stalls for fileStallTimeout · live hops are kept " .-> TRIG
